# Credentials for the imagegen tool.
# Provide only the keys for the provider(s) you want to use.
#
# 1. Copy this file:   cp tools/imagegen/.env.example tools/imagegen/.env
# 2. Fill in the values for your chosen provider(s).
# 3. The `.env` file is git-ignored — your keys never leave the machine.

# ── OpenAI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for --provider openai (gpt-image-1, dall-e-3, dall-e-2).
# Get it at: platform.openai.com → API keys → Create new secret key.
# Note: gpt-image-1 may require organization verification on your OpenAI org.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for --provider cloudflare (flux-2-dev, flux-2-klein-*, flux-1-schnell).
#   - CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: dash.cloudflare.com → your account → right sidebar
#     "Account ID" (32-char hex string).
#   - CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: dash.cloudflare.com → My Profile → API Tokens →
#     Create Token → "Custom Token" → permission "Workers AI: Edit".
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
